WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:02.800
The phone always rings
at the worst moment.

2
00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.270
Mid-rush, mid-meeting, after hours.

3
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.480
Callers stuck on hold, then gone.

4
00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:10.740
And every missed call is a
customer who'll try someone else.

5
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.430
Meet our bespoke voice agents.

6
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.890
They answer every call, day or night.

7
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.770
Train it on your business.

8
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.140
Your menus, your hours, your policies.

9
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.250
Or point it at your website.

10
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.080
It rereads your site on a schedule.

11
00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.180
So when something changes,
your agent already knows.

12
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.480
Nothing invented, nothing guessed.

13
00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:34.680
Most AI receptionists are
AI with a phone bolted on.

14
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.650
Our bespoke voice agents
are the other way round.

15
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.360
They run on Fuse 2's own UK carrier-
grade network and talk speech-to-speech,

16
00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.600
with no robotic relay in between.

17
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.700
It works with the phone
system you already have:

18
00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.290
any PBX, any SIP trunk, any number.

19
00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.080
No rip and replace.

20
00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.770
And you choose the AI behind it:

21
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.680
OpenAI, xAI or Gemini
today, with more to come,

22
00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:01.300
so you can switch when
something better arrives,

23
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.190
in over 20 languages.

24
00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.390
It connects to your booking
and business systems.

25
00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.100
When a call needs a
person, it rings ahead,

26
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.900
sums up the call and lets
you accept or reject.

27
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.420
Or it emails the details to your inbox.

28
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:16.310
You see everything:

29
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.050
live transcripts, full call history,

30
00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.000
and a summary with sentiment
and outcome after every call.

31
00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.600
And guardrails it can't
talk its way round,

32
00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.800
with our specialists watching for misuse.

33
00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:28.920
Setting up is simple.

34
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.150
Pick a template to follow the wizard

35
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.040
and let AI help write your
agent's instructions.

36
00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.020
No technical team needed.

37
00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.040
Live in days, not months.

38
00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:42.260
Your agent isn't made for your
industry. It's made for you.

39
00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.140
Your name, your way of
working, your customers.

40
00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:47.510
Our bespoke voice agents,

41
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.200
built by experts who actually know voice.

42
00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.500
Speak to the Fuse 2 team today.
